      {
         "id": "c18ec7eb-1bfb-4639-bb45-f1ad0edf104a",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "c137d968-eb5a-47e7-90b1-1c4cadd47ca9",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=c137d968-eb5a-47e7-90b1-1c4cadd47ca9",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "0cb685b3-30b9-4c4b-8b8a-cb777c51208a",
               "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
               "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Plane.html",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Plane\n\nMany times in life we try to reduce our options to only two -- or even to a single one. This seems to simplify our life, but in reality it hides what is really happening, and we may make the wrong choice.\n\nOur hands show this clearly: when we kept everything on a flat surface to count, we ignored the depth that was always there. In mathematics, a flat surface with only two dimensions is called a plane, as Figure 2 shows.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "0cb685b3-30b9-4c4b-8b8a-cb777c51208a",
                     "text": "Weisstein, Eric W.",
                     "page": "https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Plane.html",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "",
                        "year": "",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p style=\"width:100%;text-align:center;margin:0;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 200\" width=\"50%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" style=\"display:block;margin:0 auto;\"><rect x=\"2\" y=\"2\" width=\"196\" height=\"196\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"4\"/></svg></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "A square representing a plane, a flat surface with only two dimensions.",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><b>Figure 2</b>: A plane: a flat surface that has only two dimensions.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "3f90fa48-35a6-4a96-ad0a-8f1ed8c17909",
         "prev": "",
